## Suggested "reduced settings" shape

If the goal is **one view, less stuff**, I'd consolidate to roughly:

| Keep (score ≥4) | Move in-flow / onboarding | Hide or fix (score ≤2) |
|-----------------|---------------------------|------------------------|
| Save folder | Mic picker (TitleBar) | Hotkey displays → Help text only |
| Model install + Scribe model pick | Permissions (first-run + banner) | Input/output labels → fixed `in:`/`out:` |
| Press Enter after dictate | Speaker capture toggles | Dictate model override |
| Capture speaker by default + device name (mac) | Voice enrollment | Replacements tab entirely |
| Keep WAV | Theme (optional single toggle) | Voice learning toggles (inactive) |
| Permissions | | Sensitivity slider |
| Display name | | Encryption toggle |
| Update check | | Design system link |

That cuts **6 tabs → ~3 areas**: **Setup** (permissions, model, folder), **Preferences** (theme, dictate enter, keep wav, markdown), **Voice** (enrollment + display name + delete tools).

