`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- **General uses batch Save; everything else auto-saves.** That inconsistency makes General feel heavier than Voice or Models — a simplification pass could auto-save toggles there too and drop the Save button.
- **Several "settings" are config fields with no UI** (`dictate_auto_paste` always on, `preferred_input_device` only in TitleBar). The audit surface is larger than what users actually see — good sign you can delete UI without deleting capability.
- **Replacements is the only tab that's mostly author-time configuration.** Permissions and Models are setup; General/Voice are preferences; Replacements is a rules DSL — the odd one out for a "just transcribe" product.
